export const KB_RAW: ReadonlyArray<{ file: string; raw: string }> = [
  { file: "getting-around/dashboard.md", raw: "---\ntitle: The dashboard (home page)\naudience: all\nroute: /\n---\n\nThe dashboard at [Home](/) is the landing page after sign-in.\n\nTop to bottom on desktop: a navy hero (today's date, a greeting, which shift holds the county, and a count of upcoming classes), alert banners when something needs you (required training waiting, policies awaiting acknowledgement, or a push-notifications invite), a strip of featured shortcut tiles with a **Customize** pill, then Announcements, People (the employee Spotlight plus today's birthdays), and the Station Directory. The right rail has Your compliance, an MIH referral card, Upcoming Classes (with Register links), and a Call Volume tile that opens [Insights](/insights). The Training Library section at the bottom shows the three newest recordings.\n\nOn phones the same content stacks in one column, with slim shortcut strips near the top (Event equipment, MIH referral, and a compliance strip when you're caught up) and a floating **Quick Links** pill at the bottom of the screen.\n\nUseful details:\n\n- The hero's shift line (\"X Shift · Day 1/2\") comes from the live 48/96 rotation — see the shift rotation article.\n- The Station Directory rows have a **Code** button that reveals a station's door code for 20 seconds, plus the address and phone when expanded.\n- Birthdays show for teammates who left \"Show my birthday on the dashboard\" on; you can tap the heart to wish them happy birthday or leave a note.\n- Navigation: on desktop use the navy nav bar (Home, Directory, Protocols, Training, Scheduling, Equipment, Policies, Hospitals, MIH Referral, Uniforms, Systems). On phones, the ☰ menu opens the same pages. Global search is **Ctrl/Cmd+K** anywhere — it finds pages, people, hospitals, stations, classes, and recordings.\n" },
  { file: "getting-around/install-app.md", raw: "---\ntitle: Installing the portal on your phone\naudience: all\nroute: /\n---\n\nThe portal is a PWA — install it once and it opens full-screen from your home screen like a native app (\"WCEMS Portal\").\n\n**iPhone / iPad (Safari):**\n\n1. Open employee.wallercountyems.com in Safari.\n2. Tap the **Share** icon in the Safari toolbar.\n3. Choose **Add to Home Screen**, then **Add**.\n\n**Android (Chrome):**\n\n1. Open the site in Chrome.\n2. A banner — \"Install the WCEMS app\" — appears a few seconds after load; tap **Install**. (If you dismissed it, use Chrome's menu → *Add to home screen*.)\n\nA reminder banner appears on phones that haven't installed yet; the X dismisses it permanently on that device.\n\nTwo things only work well from the installed app:\n\n- **Push notifications on iPhone** require the app to be installed to the home screen first — Safari tabs can't receive them.\n- Full-screen, app-like layout with no browser bars.\n\n**Updates are automatic.** The app checks for new versions every ~20 minutes and whenever you reopen it, then switches to the new version on your next navigation or the next time you open the app — there is no \"update\" button. If a page looks stale after a release, fully close the app and reopen it.\n" },
  { file: "getting-around/profile-settings.md", raw: "---\ntitle: Your profile and settings\naudience: all\nroute: /\n---\n\nOpen your profile from the avatar in the top-right (phones: tap it, then **View profile**) or by clicking your name in the top utility bar on desktop. There's no Save button — each field saves as you change it.\n\nWhat you can edit:\n\n- **Photo** — tap the camera button (**Add photo** / **Change** / **Remove**); images up to 5 MB.\n- **Phone** (under Contact).\n- **Privacy** — two toggles: **\"Show my birthday on the dashboard\"** (your name appears in the People section on your birthday) and **\"Include me in the Employee Directory\"**.\n- **Notifications** — push notifications for new announcements (see the notifications article).\n- **Scheduling** (if you have schedule access) — text-message opt-in and mobile number, a per-alert-type Push/Email/Text grid, your shift highlight color, and unavailable days. These have their own **Save settings** button.\n\nWhat you can't edit:\n\n- **Station and Shift are automatic** — they come from the schedule's rotation. If your seat changes, they update on their own; part-timers without a rotation seat show no shift. Don't ask an admin to type these.\n- **Birthday** is read-only — ask an admin to correct the date itself.\n- Name, email, role, title, or fuel card: talk to an admin.\n\nYour **fuel number** is in the avatar dropdown (phones): it shows masked as ••••••, tap it to reveal for 20 seconds, with a copy button while visible.\n\nSign-in is your @wallercountyems.com Microsoft account — the portal has no separate password to change. **Sign out** lives in the avatar dropdown, the profile footer, and the desktop utility bar.\n" },
  { file: "getting-around/notifications.md", raw: "---\ntitle: Push notifications\naudience: all\nroute: /\n---\n\nThe portal can push notifications to your phone or computer for **new announcements** and, if you use the scheduling module, for **schedule alerts** (approvals, trades, reminders, time verification).\n\n**Turn on announcement notifications:**\n\n1. Watch for the \"Stay in the loop\" banner on the dashboard and tap **Turn on**, or\n2. Open your profile (avatar → **View profile**) → **Notifications** → check **\"Push notifications for new announcements\"**.\n\nOn iPhone you must install the portal to your home screen first (Share → Add to Home Screen) — Safari tabs can't receive push. If the checkbox says \"Blocked by your browser,\" enable notifications for the site in your browser settings, then come back.\n\nSubscriptions are **per device and per browser** — turn it on separately on your phone and your computer. Untick the box to stop notifications on that device.\n\nWhat announcement pushes look like: \"{Category}: {Title}\" with the first line of the post; tapping one opens the announcements section of the dashboard.\n\n**Schedule alerts** are configured separately in your profile's **Scheduling** section (or in [Schedule](/schedule) → My schedule → My settings): a grid of Push / Email / Text per alert type — request decisions, schedule changes, open shifts & page-outs, trades, shift reminders, time verification, and scheduler announcements. Shift reminders default to 12 hours before your shift. Text messages require opting in and saving a mobile number; emails come from schedule@wallercountyems.com.\n" },
  { file: "getting-around/quick-links.md", raw: "---\ntitle: Quick links and featured shortcuts\naudience: all\nroute: /\n---\n\nQuick links are the catalog of outside systems (Outlook, ESO, Paycom, Supply Portal, Protocols shortcuts, and so on). They appear in three places:\n\n- **Featured shortcuts strip** on the dashboard — your personal picks.\n- **Quick Links pill** floating at the bottom on phones — the full catalog with search.\n- **Systems menu** in the desktop nav bar (and the external-systems links in the top utility bar).\n\n**Customize your featured strip:**\n\n1. On the dashboard, tap **Customize** on the shortcuts strip.\n2. Pick up to 4 links (\"{n} / 4 selected\"). **Schedule** and **Hospitals** always stay as the first and last tiles.\n3. **Save**. (**Reset** returns you to the role defaults — for crew that's Outlook, Protocols, Employee Shoutout, and Supply Portal.)\n\n**Pin links in the phone dock:**\n\n1. Tap the **Quick Links** pill at the bottom of the dashboard.\n2. Search or browse by category; tap the pin icon on any link.\n3. Pinned links gather in a **Pinned** section at the top of the dock.\n\nPins and featured picks are personal to you. The catalog itself (which links exist, their names and categories) is managed by admins — if a system you use is missing, ask an admin to add it, or use \"Report an issue\"/\"Suggest a link\" in the page footer.\n" },
  { file: "getting-around/announcements.md", raw: "---\ntitle: Announcements\naudience: all\nroute: /\n---\n\nAnnouncements live in a carousel on the [dashboard](/) — there's no separate announcements page. The carousel rotates on its own every few seconds; use the arrows or dots to move manually (that pauses the auto-rotation), or the play/pause button. On phones, swipe between slides.\n\nReading:\n\n- Longer posts show a snippet with **\"Read the full story →\"** — tap it for the full post (title, category, date, author, image, and full text).\n- Tap an announcement's image to see it full-size.\n- When comments are enabled on a post, the detail view has a comment thread — type in \"Add a comment…\" and post. (Shared kiosk logins can't comment.)\n\nNew announcements trigger a push notification — \"{Category}: {Title}\" — on every device that opted in (see the push notifications article). Only new posts notify; edits don't.\n\nPosting, editing, archiving, and deleting announcements is admin-only — crew who want something announced should send it to an admin or the appropriate supervisor.\n" },
  { file: "getting-around/directory.md", raw: "---\ntitle: Employee directory\naudience: all\nroute: /directory\n---\n\nThe [Employee Directory](/directory) lists colleagues' name, photo, title, station, shift, phone, and email. Find it in the nav (desktop: Directory; phones: ☰ → Employee Directory) or with Ctrl/Cmd+K search.\n\nUsing it:\n\n1. Search by name, title, station, or email.\n2. Narrow with the filter pills: Shift (All + each letter), Station, and Role.\n3. Each card has a phone button (tap to call) and an email button — there's no separate detail page.\n\nOnly people who opted in are listed: the toggle is **\"Include me in the Employee Directory\"** in your profile (avatar → View profile → Privacy). Shared kiosk accounts never appear. If you just opted out, the list updates after the page reloads.\n\nFuel numbers and door codes are never shown in the directory.\n" },
  { file: "getting-around/gallery.md", raw: "---\ntitle: Photo gallery (Around the County)\naudience: all\nroute: /gallery\n---\n\nThe photo gallery at [Around the County](/gallery) collects agency photos — outreach events, stations, training, crews. Reach it from the desktop footer link \"Around the County\" or by searching \"Photo Gallery\" (Ctrl/Cmd+K).\n\nEveryone can browse, filter by tag (All, WCEMS, Outreach, Stations, Training, Crew, plus custom tags), heart a photo, and comment on it — tap a photo to open it full-size with its caption and comment thread. Shared kiosk accounts can look but can't heart or comment.\n\n**Uploading is admin-only.** Admins use the **Upload photo** button: choose a JPG/PNG/WebP up to 8 MB, add a caption (up to 80 characters) and a tag, then **Upload**. Admins can also delete photos; comment authors (or admins) can delete comments. There are no albums — tags are the only grouping.\n\nIf you have photos worth sharing, send them to an admin to post.\n" },
  { file: "getting-around/admin-staff.md", raw: "---\ntitle: Admin Staff contacts\naudience: all\nroute: /admin-staff\n---\n\nThe [Admin Staff](/admin-staff) page is the direct-contact list for WCEMS administrative staff — each card shows a title, name, phone (tap to call), email, and any notes. Use it when you need \"the right person\" for HR, payroll, scheduling, clinical development, supplies, and similar questions.\n\nFind it from the phone menu (☰ → Admin Staff) or Ctrl/Cmd+K search — on desktop there's no nav entry, so search is the quickest path.\n\nAdmins maintain the list at [Manage Admin Staff](/admin/admin-staff): add entries (Title, Name, Email, Phone, Notes, and an \"Active (visible to crew)\" toggle), edit, reorder with the arrows, or delete. Changes show up for everyone in real time.\n" },
  { file: "getting-around/kudos.md", raw: "---\ntitle: Kudos and the employee Spotlight\naudience: all\nroute: /\n---\n\nWant to recognize a teammate? Send a **shoutout** — it's a short external form (Employee Shoutout on Jotform), not an in-portal page.\n\nWays to open the form:\n\n- Dashboard → People section → Spotlight card → **\"Send a shoutout →\"**\n- The **Employee Shoutout** tile on the featured shortcuts strip (a crew default)\n- The Quick Links dock or Systems menu, under the shoutout link\n\nThe form asks for your name and email, the recipient's name and email, and the kudos text. Submissions land with admin staff automatically (they're stored and emailed to the review team) — nothing posts publicly on its own.\n\nFrom there, an admin can turn a great write-up into the dashboard **Spotlight**: the featured recognition card in the People section, with the person's name, role, tenure, a blurb, and optionally a longer story and photo. One spotlight is active at a time, and its \"Congratulations & comments\" thread notifies the person being recognized.\n\nSo: submit shoutouts freely — the best ones become the Spotlight everyone sees on the [dashboard](/).\n" },
  { file: "getting-around/insights.md", raw: "---\ntitle: Call volume insights\naudience: all\nroute: /insights\n---\n\n[Call Volume](/insights) shows the agency's monthly run numbers. Open it from the dashboard's Call Volume tile, the phone menu (☰ → Call Volume Insights), or search.\n\nWhat's there:\n\n- A **Month** picker (defaults to the latest month with data).\n- Stat cards: Total Calls, Avg Response, In District, Out of District, Patients, Transports, UHU, Air Transports.\n- Three tabs: **Trend** (monthly call-volume line), **By Unit** (runs, share, and average response per unit), and **By Zone** (a donut of scene zones).\n\nThe dashboard tile shows the current month's total with a sparkline and the change versus last month.\n\nData comes from the agency's monthly run report, entered by admins — if a month is missing or looks off, let an admin know. The trend chart needs at least two months of data before it draws.\n" },
  { file: "schedule/shift-rotation.md", raw: "---\ntitle: How the shift rotation works (and which shift works a date)\naudience: all\nroute: /schedule\n---\n\nWCEMS runs a **48/96 rotation** with three platoons — A, B, and C Shift. Each shift works two consecutive 24-hour days (starting at **0600 Central**), then has four days off. Shift change is 0600, so \"today's shift\" before 6 a.m. is still yesterday's platoon.\n\n**The pattern** repeats every 6 days: B, B, C, C, A, A — anchored at **Monday, April 6, 2026 = B Shift, Day 1**.\n\nTo work out which shift holds a given date:\n\n1. Count the days from April 6, 2026 to the date (in Central time).\n2. Take that count mod 6.\n3. Map it: 0 → B (Day 1), 1 → B (Day 2), 2 → C (Day 1), 3 → C (Day 2), 4 → A (Day 1), 5 → A (Day 2).\n\nWorked example: October 24, 2026 is 201 days after the anchor; 201 mod 6 = 3 → **C Shift, Day 2**.\n\nWhere to see it in the app:\n\n- The dashboard hero says \"X-Shift holds the county today\" with the duty day.\n- [Schedule](/schedule) → Day board header shows \"X Shift on duty\" with the actual roster — always trust the board over mental math, because trades, time off, and unit-specific patterns change who's really on.\n\nYour own shift letter (in your profile and the directory) comes from your rotation seat automatically.\n" },
  { file: "schedule/schedule-basics.md", raw: "---\ntitle: Reading the schedule\naudience: all\nroute: /schedule\n---\n\nOpen [Schedule](/schedule) from the nav (\"Scheduling\"). On desktop it runs as its own app with a navy bar — use **Employee Portal** on the left to come back. Phones get a swipeable tab strip.\n\n**Boards** (Schedule menu): Month, Day, Week, and Pay period. Desktop opens on Month; phones open on Day. Move with Previous / **Today** / Next or the jump-to-date picker.\n\n**Who's working today:** the Day board. The header names the on-duty shift and counts open seats; below, each station's units list their seats — name, credential, and start–end times, with \"R\" marking a regular rotation seat. Open seats are tappable (see the extra hours article for pickups). Boxes below the roster show Extra Hours, Trades, Time Off, Special events, and Pending Requests for that day.\n\n**Your own shifts:** the **My schedule** tab — the same views filtered to you (your days highlighted in your chosen color), a \"N shift days this month\" count, your pending requests, and the **My settings** button (notifications, text opt-in, shift highlight, unavailable days). Full-timers also see leave balances at the top: Vacation and Sick hours with the next accrual date, and **View details** opens the full ledger plus a \"How much will I have on [date]\" planner.\n\nA gold strip on the boards reminds you when shift-time confirmations or a pay-period sign-off are waiting — see the time verification article.\n\nIf the page says \"Scheduling isn't open yet,\" your account hasn't been given schedule access — ask an admin.\n" },
  { file: "schedule/time-off.md", raw: "---\ntitle: Requesting time off\naudience: all\nroute: /schedule\n---\n\nTwo ways to start, both in [Schedule](/schedule):\n\n**From the Requests tab:**\n\n1. Open **Requests** → **New request** → **Time off**.\n2. Pick a type: Vacation, Sick, Unpaid time off, Bereavement, Deployment, or Other.\n3. Either pick days under \"From my scheduled shifts\" (your next 45 days, with \"Edit time\" for partial days) or use \"Custom date\" with From/Until times.\n4. Add comments if needed and **Submit request**.\n\n**From a board:** tap your own shift → **Request time off** → type, window, comments → **Submit time-off request**.\n\nWhat happens next: the request goes to the schedulers (\"the Chief\") for approval. You'll get a push + email when it's approved or denied. Once approved, your seat shows OPEN on the boards for that window so it can be picked up.\n\nRules worth knowing:\n\n- **Vacation and Sick are balance-checked** — if the hours requested exceed what you'll have (counting accruals through the last day and anything already pending), the app blocks it and suggests shortening it or using Unpaid time off.\n- **Cancel while pending** from My schedule → \"Your pending requests\" → Cancel (or tap the Pending row on a board). After approval, only a scheduler can change or remove it — ask them.\n- Balances show at the top of **My schedule** for full-time employees (hours, with accrual per pay period based on tenure). **View details** opens the ledger and planner.\n- To just warn schedulers you can't work a day (no time off needed), use \"Mark a day off unavailable\" — see the availability article.\n" },
  { file: "schedule/shift-trades.md", raw: "---\ntitle: Shift trades (swaps and giveaways)\naudience: all\nroute: /schedule\n---\n\nTrades live on the **Trades** tab of [Schedule](/schedule). Two kinds:\n\n- **Give away** — anyone qualified can claim your shift.\n- **Swap** — you want a shift back in return.\n\n**Posting:**\n\n1. Trades → **Post a shift** (or tap your shift on a board → \"Post as a trade (swap)\" / \"Give this shift away\").\n2. Pick the type, your shift (next 120 days), and where it goes: **the trade board** (anyone can respond) or **a specific person**.\n3. Optionally trade part of the shift (From/Until), add comments, then **Post to the board** / **Send the request**.\n\n**Responding:**\n\n- Giveaway: tap **Claim** — first claim wins and goes straight to the Chief for approval.\n- Swap: tap **Offer a shift**, pick one of yours, **Send offer**. The poster reviews offers and accepts or declines; an accepted deal then goes to the Chief.\n\n**Nothing changes the calendar until a scheduler approves it.** Agreed deals show \"Awaiting Chief approval\"; after approval both calendars rewrite automatically and both members get a push + email.\n\nRules the app enforces: trades close at shift start; you must be qualified for the seat (both directions on a swap); one offer per person per posting; event assignments can only be given away whole. You can withdraw a posting or an offer any time before it's accepted. The Trades tab badge counts items waiting on you.\n" },
  { file: "schedule/availability.md", raw: "---\ntitle: Marking a day unavailable\naudience: all\nroute: /schedule\n---\n\nIf you just need the schedulers to know you can't work a certain day — no time-off request, no balance involved — mark it unavailable:\n\n1. Open [Schedule](/schedule) → **Requests** → **New request** → **Time off**.\n2. Choose **\"Mark a day off unavailable\"**.\n3. Pick the date, optionally add a reason, and tap **Mark unavailable**.\n\nIt saves instantly — no approval needed. If a scheduler later tries to assign you that day, they get a warning first.\n\nYour marked days are listed right there under \"Your unavailable days\" (each with a **Remove** button) and in **My schedule → My settings → Unavailable days**.\n\nThat's the whole availability feature: there's no separate \"available to work\" signup. If you're part-time and want shifts, watch for open seats and page-outs instead — see the extra hours and open shifts article.\n" },
  { file: "schedule/time-verification.md", raw: "---\ntitle: Time verification and pay-period sign-off\naudience: all\nroute: /schedule\n---\n\nPayroll runs on verified times, in three layers. You'll get push + email prompts (never texts) and a gold reminder strip on the [Schedule](/schedule) boards; there's also a pop-up when something's waiting.\n\n**1. After each shift — confirm your times.** Open My schedule → \"Verify your shift times.\" For each day you can tap:\n\n- **My times are right** — done.\n- **I worked extra** — opens the extra-hours form.\n- **I left early / time off** — opens the time-off form.\n- **Something else is off** — type a note and **Send to the schedulers** (files a time discrepancy for them to fix).\n\n**2. Supervisors attest the trucks.** The morning after, on-duty supervisors confirm each truck's roster matched reality (\"Roster matched\" or flag it with a note). Crew don't do anything here.\n\n**3. Pay-period sign-off.** The Sunday after a period closes you'll be prompted (\"Approve your pay-period hours\", with a last call at 9:00 — **due by 10:00 that morning**; HR keys Paycom Monday). Review the day table and either **Approve — my times are right** or **Something's wrong** (pick the day, add a note, send). Once signed off, you can't change it yourself — contact a scheduler.\n\nPay periods run Sunday–Saturday (two weeks); payday is the Friday after the period ends. Questions about a specific discrepancy go to the schedulers via the \"Something's wrong\" flow, which files it directly in their queue.\n" },
  { file: "schedule/extra-hours.md", raw: "---\ntitle: Extra hours, open shifts, and page-outs\naudience: all\nroute: /schedule\n---\n\n**Claim an open seat:** open seats show on every board of [Schedule](/schedule) (the Day board header counts them). Tap one → **Request this shift**. Schedulers approve pickups first-come-first-listed; you must hold the seat's required credential (if not, a scheduler can still assign you directly).\n\n**Request extra hours you worked or will work:**\n\n1. **Requests** → **New request** → **Extra hours**.\n2. Fill in the window (Starts/From/Ends/Until), Unit, Position, and a time type — Regular, Instructor, Meeting, Special Event, or Deployment.\n3. Add comments and submit; a scheduler approves it onto that day's **Extra Hours** box.\n\nLong windows trigger warnings (and anything over 48 hours is rejected).\n\n**Special events** (standbys, games, fair coverage): schedulers post them with Paramedic/Attendant seats. Open event rows show on the Day board — claim them like open shifts. If you're assigned directly, you'll get a \"You were assigned\" notification, and an equipment-check reminder fires when the event starts.\n\n**Page-outs:** when supervisors need coverage fast, they send a page-out (push/email/text) that can include the open shifts — tap a shift in the message to open the pickup flow. Read past ones under the **Messages** tab. Make sure your notification settings (\"Open shifts & page-outs\") are on if you want these — see your profile's Scheduling section.\n" },
  { file: "training/classes.md", raw: "---\ntitle: Upcoming classes — browsing, registering, cancelling\naudience: all\nroute: /training\n---\n\n[Upcoming Classes](/training) lists every scheduled class — AHA card classes, CE lectures, and calendar events — grouped by month, synced automatically every 15 minutes from Wix Bookings and the education calendar. Rows show the date, time, location, instructor, and for seat-limited classes a \"Registered X / Y\" count.\n\n**Registering:**\n\n- **AHA card classes** (CPR/ACLS/PALS): tap **Register** — it opens the Internal Education page on wallercountyems.com, where you book through the website. Use your account there to manage or cancel the booking.\n- **CE lectures**: tap **Register** — a short form asks your name, work email, certification level, and whether you'll attend in person or virtually (Teams). Your CE certificate is emailed to the work email you enter.\n- Calendar-only events have no registration — just show up.\n\n**Cancelling:** there's no cancel button in the portal. For a card class, cancel the booking on the website where you registered; for a lecture, contact the training team (see [Admin Staff](/admin-staff)) so your seat opens up.\n\n**On class day** you'll usually scan a QR code to check in; card classes also collect your eCard email and mailing details. After class, the evaluation (and quiz, if the lecture has one) are required before CE credit is awarded.\n\nThe **Skills** card on this page (shown to supervisors, FTOs, and evaluators) opens the skills boards — see the skills article.\n" },
  { file: "training/recordings.md", raw: "---\ntitle: Training Library (recordings)\naudience: all\nroute: /training/recordings\n---\n\nThe [Training Library](/training/recordings) holds past training videos — protocol updates, Doc Day recordings, skills refreshers, and more.\n\nFinding something:\n\n1. Search by title, instructor, topic, or tag.\n2. Or browse: category chips (Doc Day, Protocol Updates, Skills, Community Paramedicine, Operations, Equipment, Annual / Required…) with a \"Recently Added\" strip of the newest uploads.\n3. Sort by Newest, Oldest, Most viewed, or A→Z.\n\nTap a recording to play it right in the portal — YouTube, SharePoint, and direct videos all play in place. Items tagged **Required** are cross-listed required-training modules: tapping one takes you to its module page (with the attestation flow) instead of a plain player.\n\nRecordings are posted by admins via [Manage Training Library](/admin/training-recordings). If a class you missed isn't in the library, ask the training team whether a recording exists.\n" },
  { file: "training/required-training.md", raw: "---\ntitle: Required training — watching and signing off\naudience: all\nroute: /training/required\n---\n\n[Required Training](/training/required) lists compliance modules assigned to you by the Chief and Medical Director, split into **Outstanding** and **Completed**, each with its due date and status (Not started / In progress / Overdue). A dashboard banner nags while anything is outstanding.\n\n**Completing a video module:**\n\n1. Open the module and press play.\n2. Watch it through — **skipping ahead is disabled**: scrubbing forward snaps you back to your furthest point (rewinding is fine). The progress bar shows \"Watch progress N%\".\n3. When the video ends, the **Attestation of Completion** unlocks: read the attestation points, sign the signature pad, and tap **Submit attestation**.\n4. Your certificate PDF downloads automatically, and you can re-download it from the module page any time.\n\n**External-course modules** (\"External course\") unlock the attestation when you tap **Open the course** — complete the course on the external site, come back, sign, and submit.\n\nWorth knowing:\n\n- Watch progress follows you across devices — start on one device and the video resumes at your furthest point on another, and a video watched to the end unlocks the attestation everywhere (so you can watch on a laptop and sign on your phone).\n- After you've completed a module you can re-watch and scrub freely.\n- Who gets assigned what is set by admins (by role/shift/employment type, or tied to a scheduled event — event crews get push reminders).\n- If an admin marked you complete (e.g., you attended a live session), it shows in Completed without a video step.\n\nYour completion record (timestamp + signature) is the compliance proof; the certificate is your copy.\n" },
  { file: "training/ce-certificates.md", raw: "---\ntitle: CE certificates and your training records\naudience: all\nroute: /clinical-development\n---\n\n**To submit a CE card or certificate you earned: upload it in Paycom** — the portal itself has no employee upload for certificates. Records are imported from Paycom into your clinical file on the next records import, so a copy uploaded there gets picked up automatically. (If you're unsure where in Paycom, ask HR via [Admin Staff](/admin-staff).)\n\n**Certificates from WCEMS lectures** are generated by the training team after the class — you qualify by checking in, submitting the evaluation, and passing the quiz if there is one. They're emailed to the work email you registered with.\n\n**Where your records live:** your clinical file. On [My Progress](/clinical-development) you can see:\n\n- Your credential dates and compliance status (cards, jurisprudence, and so on).\n- **My documents** — files the Clinical Development staff have shared to your file, which can include CE certificates and cert cards they've filed for you.\n- Certificates from required-training modules download at completion and can be re-downloaded from each module's page under [Required Training](/training/required).\n\nIf a card you renewed still shows the old date, give the import a few days or contact Clinical Development — they can file the card directly to your record.\n" },
  { file: "training/protocol-exams.md", raw: "---\ntitle: Taking a protocol exam\naudience: all\nroute: /clinical-development\n---\n\nProtocol exams are proctored, timed online tests used at credentialing steps (for example P1C → P1). You don't sign up for one — Clinical Development assigns it to you.\n\n**Taking one:**\n\n1. Open [My Progress](/clinical-development) — your assigned exam shows as a card with **Begin exam** (or **Resume exam**).\n2. The exam is proctored: it stays locked (\"Your proctor will release this examination when you're seated and ready\") until your proctor releases it — the page unlocks by itself.\n3. Read the header (questions, time limit, passing score), then **Begin examination**. The clock starts and can't be paused.\n4. Answer one question per screen — Previous/Next, a question grid to jump around, and some \"select all that apply\" or image questions. Answers autosave every couple of seconds.\n5. **Review & submit** lists anything unanswered (unanswered scores as incorrect), then **Submit examination**. It also auto-submits at 0:00.\n\n**Results** show immediately: your score and Passed / Not passed. A pass automatically checks your protocol-exam gate and files a completion certificate to your documents. The review screen shows which questions you missed with the protocol reference to study — correct answers are never revealed.\n\nIf you don't pass, Clinical Development will arrange the retake. Questions about an assignment go to the clinical staff ([Admin Staff](/admin-staff)).\n" },
  { file: "policies/policies.md", raw: "---\ntitle: Reading and acknowledging policies\naudience: all\nroute: /policies\n---\n\n[Policies](/policies) lists the clinical, operational, HR, and general policies you're required to read and sign. Outstanding ones are flagged by a dashboard banner (\"Policies awaiting acknowledgement\") and the desktop compliance card.\n\n**To acknowledge a policy:**\n\n1. Open [Policies](/policies) and pick one under \"awaiting acknowledgement\".\n2. Read the PDF in the viewer — the progress bar tracks you (\"Reading X / Y — scroll to the end to enable acknowledgement\").\n3. When you've scrolled to the end, the three attestation checkboxes unlock:\n   - \"I have read this policy in full.\"\n   - \"I understand its contents.\"\n   - \"I know where to find this policy on the intranet.\"\n4. Check all three, sign the signature pad, and tap **Acknowledge and submit**.\n\nA signed certificate PDF downloads automatically, and you can re-download it from the policy page any time. The acknowledgement records your signature, the time, and the policy version.\n\n**Why a policy came back after you signed it:** acknowledgements are tied to a policy *version*. When an admin uploads a new revision, the version bumps and everyone must re-acknowledge — the row shows \"Update — please re-acknowledge.\" Your old signature is kept for audit; it just doesn't cover the new text.\n\nNotes: station kiosk accounts can't acknowledge (sign in with your own account), and which policies you see depends on the audience the admin set (role, shift, employment type) — \"No policies assigned to you yet\" means none currently target you.\n" },
  { file: "protocols/protocols.md", raw: "---\ntitle: Protocols, procedures, and medications\naudience: all\nroute: /protocols\n---\n\n[Protocols](/protocols) is the full 2026 protocol reference — a dark, full-screen app of its own. Get back to the portal with the **Portal** pill at the top left.\n\nBottom navigation: **Protocols | Procedures | Tools | More**.\n\n- **Protocols** (the 2.x items) and **Procedures** (the 1.x items) — browse \"By Number\" (default) or \"By Category\", or search. A protocol page has an Adult/Pediatric toggle and level tabs (ECA/EMT, AEMT, Paramedic — higher levels show the lower levels' steps first), plus CRITERIA, NOTES, and MED CONTROL boxes. Drug mentions are highlighted and protocol references are tappable links.\n- **More** holds **Medications** (a drug reference with indications, contraindications, side effects, dosage & routes, and minimum certification per drug — plus the formulary table), the **Equipment** supply list, the complete signed **2026 Protocol Manual** PDF, and **Download for Offline Use** — tap that once so protocols work with no signal.\n\nThe assistant can quote the protocol book and drug reference **verbatim** (live lookups of the signed text, always cited with the protocol number and name plus a link to the page) — but it never turns protocol text into its own advice, and it is not medical direction: always verify in the protocol itself. For calculators and reference tools (burn, APGAR, stroke, STEMI, and more), see the protocol tools article.\n" },
  { file: "protocols/tools.md", raw: "---\ntitle: Protocol tools and calculators\naudience: all\nroute: /protocols\n---\n\nOpen [Protocols](/protocols) → the **Tools** tab at the bottom. Each tool opens as a pop-up sheet (close with ✕):\n\nClinical calculators:\n\n- **STEMI Reference** — heart diagram, 12-lead placement, STEMI criteria, and Sgarbossa (original + modified).\n- **Stroke Assessment** — Cincinnati (CPSS) and the VAN large-vessel-occlusion screen.\n- **Burn Calculator** — Rule of Nines and a TBSA calculator with fluid rate by age.\n\nOB / neonatal:\n\n- **Contraction Tracker** — tap to time contractions (duration + frequency), export the log as PDF.\n- **Delivery Documentation** — birth time, APGAR at 1 & 5 minutes, complications, exportable delivery report.\n- **Newborn APGAR** — APGAR scoring with due-time reminders and PDF export.\n\n(The delivery and APGAR tools share their data, so you don't enter the birth time twice. OB tool data lives only in that tab — it clears on reload, so export the PDF before closing.)\n\nReference sheets: **RASS Scale**, **H's and T's**, **Wong-Baker Pain Scale**, **Atropine Dosing** (organophosphate/SLUDGE), and the **SAM Splint User Guide**.\n\nThese tools support documentation and recall — they are not medical direction.\n" },
  { file: "equipment/checkout.md", raw: "---\ntitle: Event equipment check-out and shift checks\naudience: all\nroute: /equipment\n---\n\n[Equipment](/equipment) tracks event gear chain-of-custody: what's on the shelf, out at events, in transit, or reported not found. Anyone can view the board, look up an item by its PSTrax tag (\"Search tag, name, or type…\" or /equipment/item/TAG), and see custody history.\n\n**Checking out** is for equipment handlers (supervisors, admins, and granted staff): **Check out equipment** → pick items → say what it's for, which truck (by truck number), and when. A multi-night deployment uses the **Extended assignment** toggle with From/Through dates. Delivery hand-offs capture the receiver's signature on your phone.\n\n**What regular crews do:**\n\n- **Confirm it's here** when gear arrives, and run **Start-of-shift** / **End-of-shift checks** on extended assignments. Every item starts as \"here\" — tap anything that isn't to mark it Not found (a note saying what's missing and where you looked is required).\n- **The end-of-shift check requires a photo** of where you're leaving the gear. Start-of-shift doesn't.\n- **Close out the event** when it's truly over — tick \"The event is over — this equipment won't be needed again.\" If another crew works it tomorrow, don't close; they'll check the gear when they come on. Closed too soon? **Reopen the event** undoes it.\n- A **Print card** PDF travels with the gear (QR code + item checklist), and **Send to crew** shares the link.\n\nMissing or damaged gear: mark it Not found during a check with a note, and tell your supervisor right away. Handlers record pickups, drop-offs at Admin, and write-offs.\n\nYou'll get a push reminder — \"Event equipment check\" — when a scheduled event assignment starts. Shared kiosk logins can view but can't record custody.\n" },
  { file: "places/hospitals.md", raw: "---\ntitle: Hospital directory and door codes\naudience: all\nroute: /hospitals\n---\n\n[Hospitals](/hospitals) is the receiving-facility directory — 20+ hospitals from the Texas Medical Center out to Bryan/College Station and Brenham, sorted by trauma level by default.\n\nFinding the right facility:\n\n1. Search by name, address, or notes.\n2. Filter with the chips: trauma level (All, Trauma I–IV), plus Stroke: Comprehensive, Stroke: Primary, PCI Capable, Pediatric, and Maternal.\n3. The Sort menu offers Trauma level (default), Name, Stroke level, or PCI capable first.\n\nTap a hospital to expand it: capability chips (stroke, PCI, maternal, NICU, pediatric), the address (opens your map app), notes, and the door codes.\n\n**Door codes:** each hospital's **ER door** and **EMS room** codes have a **Reveal** button — the code shows for 20 seconds with a draining bar, then hides itself (tap again to hide sooner). Some facilities are marked \"Ring bell\" instead of having a code. The assistant never repeats codes — always read them from the hospital card.\n\n**If a code changed:** anyone signed in can fix it — tap the pencil next to the code, type the new one, and save. Every change is logged with your name and the time, and the card shows \"Updated by … · when\".\n\nHospital details themselves (names, capabilities, addresses) are managed by admins at [Manage Hospitals](/admin/hospitals).\n" },
  { file: "places/stations.md", raw: "---\ntitle: Station directory and door codes\naudience: all\nroute: /\n---\n\nStation info lives in the **Station Directory** section of the [dashboard](/) — there's no separate stations page. Jump to it from search (Ctrl/Cmd+K → \"Station Directory\" or a station's name) or the phone menu's \"On this page → Stations\" while on the dashboard.\n\nEach station row shows:\n\n- A **Code** button that reveals the door code for 20 seconds (a draining bar shows the time; tap again to hide early). Stations marked **App Access** unlock another way and have no code to reveal.\n- Expand the row for the address (opens your map app) and phone (tap to call).\n\n**If a door code changed:** tap **Update code** on the expanded row, type the new code, and save — any signed-in user can do this, and every change is stamped with your name and time and kept in an audit log.\n\nThe assistant never repeats door codes — read them from the station row.\n\nYour own station assignment (shown in your profile) isn't set here — it comes automatically from your rotation seat in the schedule. Station records themselves (addresses, phones, names) are managed by admins at [Manage Stations](/admin/stations).\n" },
  { file: "clinical/clinical-development.md", raw: "---\ntitle: Clinical Development and My Progress\naudience: all\nroute: /clinical-development\n---\n\nClinical Development tracks every provider's credentialing — phases (NEOP Academy → Field Training Rotation → P1 Attendant → P2 In-Charge, with an optional P3 FTO track), certification cards, license dates, and field training.\n\nWhat you see depends on your role (the nav entry under **Training** changes accordingly):\n\n- **Most employees** get **My Progress** at [/clinical-development](/clinical-development): your current phase with a progress bar, your gates and compliance detail (read-only), assigned protocol exams, **My documents** (files clinical staff shared to you), **My FTEP reports** (with a banner when one needs your signature), **Messages** with the clinical team, program resources, any 2026 protocol skills still owed, and the Evaluate-my-FTO card.\n- **Supervisors and FTOs** land on the FTEP section at [/clinical/ftep](/clinical/ftep) — see the FTEP article.\n- **Clinical editors** (granted staff) get the full Clinical Development console at [/clinical](/clinical): Today (work queue), Board (compliance grid), People (employee files), FTEP, Submissions, and Exams.\n\nIf My Progress says \"No pipeline record yet,\" your record appears automatically once you're on the roster — ask the Clinical Development Officer if it doesn't.\n\nQuestions about *why* a gate or phase shows a certain way go to the clinical staff — the assistant can explain where things are, but not individual credentialing decisions.\n" },
  { file: "clinical/ftep-trainees.md", raw: "---\ntitle: FTEP — field training, DORs and ICRs\naudience: all\nroute: /clinical/ftep\n---\n\nFTEP (Field Training & Evaluation Program) is run from [/clinical/ftep](/clinical/ftep) by FTOs, supervisors, and clinical staff. Trainees interact with it through [My Progress](/clinical-development).\n\n**For FTOs and supervisors:** the FTEP home groups trainees by track (new program, legacy, P2→P3 ride-up, AEMT upgrade). Each trainee's **Actions** menu starts a **Daily Observation Report** (one per training day, reviewed with the trainee before end of shift) or an **Individual Call Report** (one per evaluated call), shows their schedule/progress and what's still needed, and opens their message thread.\n\nWriting a report: rate every category 1–5 or N.O.; anything below 3 needs a comment, and a 1 needs a documented situation. ICRs can be flagged to count toward the 10 required scored ALS call evaluations. Drafts autosave — **Save draft — finish later** — then **Review & sign**: the trainee reviews it and both sign on your device. If the trainee can't sign right then (asleep at shift change), tick the exception box and submit — they'll be prompted to review and sign later.\n\n**For trainees:** your reports appear under **My FTEP reports** on [My Progress](/clinical-development), with a banner when one needs your signature — open it, read the PDF, and **Sign & save**. Program documents (guide, handbook, workbook, blank forms) are under **Program resources**, and the **Messages** thread reaches your FTO and the clinical team (posts notify everyone on the thread).\n\nSome FTEP paperwork (certain evaluation forms) is still submitted via Jotform; clinical staff review those under Submissions and accept them into your file.\n" },
  { file: "clinical/fto-eval.md", raw: "---\ntitle: Trainee evaluation of your FTO\naudience: all\nroute: /clinical-development/fto-eval\n---\n\nAt each phase transition (for example after passing a protocol test), trainees are asked to evaluate their Field Training Officer. You'll see a card on [My Progress](/clinical-development) — \"Fill it out now\" when one is owed — or you can open the [FTO evaluation](/clinical-development/fto-eval) directly any time.\n\nThe form:\n\n1. The FTO being evaluated is filled in automatically.\n2. Rate 8 areas from 1–5 (all required).\n3. Four optional written questions — honest specifics help the program most.\n4. Signature is **optional** — you may submit unsigned.\n5. Tap **Submit to the Clinical Department**.\n\nWhere it goes: **only the Clinical Development staff can read it.** Supervisors and FTOs have no access to individual submissions, and feedback reaches FTOs in aggregate and without attribution wherever possible. (Submissions are tied to your record internally so the program can track that evaluations happened — they are not posted anywhere.)\n\nIf something needs attention faster than a form, talk to the Clinical Development Officer directly — see [Admin Staff](/admin-staff).\n" },
  { file: "clinical/skills.md", raw: "---\ntitle: Skills — NEOP Skills Day and the 2026 protocol updates\naudience: all\nroute: /skills\n---\n\nThere are two skills boards; the **Skills** card/button (on [Upcoming Classes](/training) and in the clinical nav) opens a chooser between them.\n\n**NEOP Skills Day** ([/skills](/skills)) — new-employee academy check-offs. Evaluators (supervisors, admins, FTOs, and granted staff) pick the day, a station, and a candidate, then mark every criterion Pass or Redo (a Redo needs a remediation note, and some actions auto-trigger remediation). When everything's marked: review the result, capture **both signatures** — trainee and evaluator — and **Submit check-off**. Any Redo makes the whole station a remediation; the second attempt revisits just those items with fresh signatures. The live board shows every trainee × station, builds signed packet PDFs, and runs the second-attempt queue. Candidates see their own results; passing every station checks their NEOP gate automatically.\n\n**2026 Protocol Updates** ([/skills/protocol-updates](/skills/protocol-updates)) — the campaign verifying the new-protocol skills for **every credentialed employee, by level** (EMT, Advanced EMT, Paramedic, Licensed Paramedic). Everyone sees \"My skills\" with each skill's status: verified, pending, or remediation. Evaluators additionally get the full board by level — tap a pending chip to run the check-off, which is laid out like the paper form: check the criteria, mark VERIFIED or REMEDIATION, and capture employee + evaluator signatures. Completed forms can be viewed, re-verified, or exported (blank PDFs and a CSV).\n\nTo get your protocol-update skills signed off, catch an evaluator on shift. Remember: completing the protocol-update *video* in [Required Training](/training/required) is a separate requirement from the hands-on skill verification.\n" },
  { file: "clinical/mih-referral.md", raw: "---\ntitle: MIH patient referral\naudience: all\nroute: /mih-referral\n---\n\nTo refer a patient to Mobile Integrated Healthcare (the community paramedic program), open [MIH Referral](/mih-referral) — any signed-in employee can submit one.\n\nWays in: the dashboard's \"Refer a patient to MIH → Start a referral\" card, the mobile quick strip, or the nav (\"MIH Referral\" on desktop, \"MIH Patient Referral\" in the phone menu).\n\nThe page embeds the Patient Referral form — fill it out and submit right there. If the form doesn't load, use the \"Open it in a new tab\" link on the page.\n\nThe referral goes to the MIH / community paramedic team. For questions about an existing referral or the program itself, contact the Community Paramedic via [Admin Staff](/admin-staff). (The MIH team's own tracking tool is a separate app — crews only need this referral form.)\n" },
  { file: "admin/employees.md", raw: "---\ntitle: Managing employees (and what's automated)\naudience: admin\nroute: /admin/employees\n---\n\n[Manage Employees](/admin/employees) sets each person's **role** (crew / supervisor / admin), title, employment type, account type (person vs. station kiosk), fuel #, phone, date of birth, and active flag. Search, filter by Full-Time/Part-Time, and use Edit or Deactivate per row.\n\n**Most identity data is automated — don't hand-edit it:**\n\n- **New employees appear automatically.** HR's master roster feeds a SharePoint list; the hourly roster sync creates portal accounts (first.last@wallercountyems.com, role crew), updates **employment type** from HR's Category, fills blank fuel #/DOB, and **deactivates** people who leave the roster. There is deliberately no Add button.\n- **Shift and station come from the schedule's rotation seats** (trigger + nightly sync). Editing them here gets overwritten — change the rotation template in Schedule → Setup instead.\n- **Microsoft 365 accounts** are provisioned/offboarded by the M365 lifecycle automation (licenses, groups, welcome kit, GAL contact info), and **job titles + office locations in the GAL sync daily** from the clinical pipeline and schedule. Hand-written GAL titles that don't match the managed patterns are left alone.\n\nWhat *is* yours to edit here: role, title, account type, fuel #, phone, DOB, birthday visibility, and active (for exceptions — normal departures deactivate via the roster sync).\n\nThe email field must match the person's Microsoft sign-in email until their first login (that's how the account links); after that it's contact info only.\n" },
  { file: "admin/stations-hospitals.md", raw: "---\ntitle: Managing stations and hospitals\naudience: admin\nroute: /admin/stations\n---\n\n**[Manage Stations](/admin/stations):** add or edit stations — ID (fixed once created), name, address, city/ZIP, phone, map URL, door code (\"App Access\" or numeric), and the Active toggle. Deactivate hides a station from crews; delete is permanent.\n\n**[Manage Hospitals](/admin/hospitals):** add or edit hospitals — name, trauma designation, stroke designation, PCI, pediatric, maternal, NICU, address, map URL, ER door code and EMS room code (or \"No door code (ring door bell)\"), code effective date, notes, and Active.\n\nDay-to-day **door-code corrections don't need these pages** — any signed-in user can update a code inline on the dashboard Station Directory or a hospital card, and every change is logged with name and time. These admin pages are for the facility records themselves.\n\nCrews see the results at [Hospitals](/hospitals) (filterable by trauma/stroke/PCI/pediatric/maternal, sorted by trauma level) and the dashboard Station Directory.\n" },
  { file: "admin/call-volume.md", raw: "---\ntitle: Managing call volume data\naudience: admin\nroute: /admin/call-volume\n---\n\n[Manage Call Volume](/admin/call-volume) feeds the [Insights](/insights) page and the dashboard tile.\n\n**Automatic:** a daily sync reads the monthly run-report PDF from the designated \"Call Volume\" mail folder and loads the month — including replacing a month when a corrected report is emailed. Most months need no manual work.\n\n**Manual entry or corrections:** **Add a month** (defaults to the previous month) with department totals (total incidents, average response), EMS breakdowns (in/out of district, patients, transports, UHU, air transports), per-unit run counts (Medic units, Supervisor, Community Paramedic), and per-zone calls. Saving over an existing month replaces it — the form warns you. The report month itself can't be edited after saving; delete the month and re-add it.\n\nCrews see the data as soon as it saves. The trend chart needs at least two months before it draws.\n" },
  { file: "admin/announcements.md", raw: "---\ntitle: Publishing announcements\naudience: admin\nroute: /\n---\n\nAnnouncements are posted straight from the dashboard's Announcements card — tap **+ New** (admins only; there's no separate admin page).\n\nCompose: **Headline** (required), a category (Operations / Protocol / Education / Recognition / Outreach / Event / Other with custom text), the body (Bold, Italic, links, bulleted lists, with a Preview toggle), an optional image up to 5 MB, and **Allow comments** — which adds a \"Notify on new comments\" person picker so the right people hear about replies. Then **Publish**.\n\n**Publishing a new active announcement push-notifies every subscribed device** (\"{Category}: {Title}\"). Only the initial publish notifies — edits, archive/restore, and deletes are silent, so typo fixes don't re-ping the agency.\n\nEach post has Edit, **Archive** (reversible; archived posts hide from crew but stay under \"Show archived\"), Restore, and Delete (permanent). Multiple active announcements rotate in the carousel, newest first.\n\nTip: crew don't see the Announcements card at all when nothing is active, and the image shows best around a 7:5 landscape ratio (it's never cropped). For scheduling-specific blasts (page-outs with text message support), use Schedule → Page-outs instead — that's a separate system.\n" },
  { file: "admin/training-manage.md", raw: "---\ntitle: Managing classes, lectures, and the training library\naudience: admin\nroute: /training/manage\n---\n\nThree surfaces split the training admin work:\n\n**[Manage Classes](/admin/training)** (admins): the synced class calendar — Wix Bookings + the education calendar, refreshed every 15 minutes. Here you can **Sync now**, set the instructor name per session, and **Exclude** a Wix service (its sessions disappear and stay excluded) or re-include it.\n\n**[Instructor area](/training/manage)** (\"Manage Card Classes & Lectures\" — gated by the training-instructor list, separate from portal roles): the full class workflow. **Create** publishes an AHA card class (creates the Wix booking) or a CE lecture (in-app registration). **Controls** per course: check-in/evaluation toggles, QR codes (Check-In, Eval, Quiz, Engage), edit details (date changes move the Wix event too), AHA roster PDF, Award CE Credits (generates certificates for qualified attendees — checked in + eval, quiz passed if required), Close Course, and Cancel Course (cancels the Wix event; Wix notifies bookers). **Registrations**, **Rosters/Evals exports** (archived to the record store), and **Access** (training admins only) — add instructors with their AHA number and authorized disciplines.\n\n**[Manage Training Library](/admin/training-recordings)** (admins): post recordings — title, instructor, category, tags, video source (Wix Media / SharePoint / YouTube unlisted / direct URL), optional thumbnail, role visibility, and Published. View counts show per row.\n\nRequired-training modules are separate — see the required training admin article.\n" },
  { file: "admin/required-training.md", raw: "---\ntitle: Managing required training\naudience: admin\nroute: /admin/required-training\n---\n\n[Manage Required Training](/admin/required-training) creates and tracks compliance modules.\n\n**New training:** title, description, the content source — YouTube, Cloudflare Stream, direct MP4, SharePoint, or **External course (link)** — approximate duration, a **Required by** date (blank = ongoing), the attestation statement (editable, with defaults), an optional **thumbnail** (shows on crew cards and the module page; max 5 MB), **\"Also show in Training Library\"** (cross-lists it with a Required tag), and Active.\n\n**Audience** has two modes:\n\n- **Everyone matching filters** — role, shift, and employment-type chips; an empty axis means \"any\", so no chips at all = the whole agency.\n- **Scheduled on an event** — the audience is whoever is on a schedule event in a date window, kept current automatically; event crews get an assignment notice and a reminder ~2 days before their shift. (Filter-based modules have no automatic reminder — the dashboard banner does that work.)\n\n**The roster** (per module): completion %, filters, a per-person **Required?** override (force-include or exclude anyone), **Mark complete** with a note (\"Attended A-shift Teams session…\"), **Export sign-off sheet (PDF)** with everyone's signature images, and **CSV**.\n\nThe anti-skip video player, attestation signature, and auto-downloaded certificates are built in — see the crew-facing required training article for the completion flow.\n" },
  { file: "admin/policies.md", raw: "---\ntitle: Managing policies and sign-off rosters\naudience: admin\nroute: /admin/policies\n---\n\n[Manage Policies](/admin/policies) publishes policies and tracks acknowledgements.\n\n**New policy:** title, category (Clinical / Operational / HR / General), summary, effective date, review cycle (Annual / Biennial / As needed — informational, nothing auto-re-prompts), an audience (role/shift/employment chips; empty = everyone), the attestation statement, and Active. After saving, attach the document with **Upload PDF** on the row.\n\n**Versioning is the key mechanic:** the first upload is v1. **Replace PDF** bumps the version, keeps every older file and every old acknowledgement for audit, and flips everyone back to outstanding — crews see \"Update — please re-acknowledge\" and the dashboard banner returns. Editing the title, summary, audience, or attestation does **not** bump the version — only a new PDF does.\n\n**The roster** (per policy): acknowledged %, stale and outstanding counts, per-person status chips (Signed / Admin-marked / Stale (vN) / Not signed), the same per-person require/exclude override as required training, **Mark acknowledged** with a note (\"Signed paper copy on file\"), and PDF/CSV exports — the PDF includes signature images; stale counts as not signed.\n\nCrews read and sign at [Policies](/policies): scroll-to-end gate, three attestation checkboxes, signature, auto-downloaded certificate. Deleting a policy removes all its acknowledgements — archive by unticking Active instead when in doubt.\n" },
  { file: "admin/kudos.md", raw: "---\ntitle: Kudos inbox and the Spotlight\naudience: admin\nroute: /admin/kudos\n---\n\n[Kudos](/admin/kudos) is the inbox for Employee Shoutout submissions (the external Jotform). Each card shows who it's for, who sent it, the date, and \"Read the full kudos\" — submissions also arrive by email to the review team.\n\nTwo actions per submission:\n\n- **Turn into spotlight** — opens the Spotlight editor prefilled with the recipient and the write-up, ready to polish: name, role/title, tenure, a short blurb, an optional full story and photo, then **Publish**. The Spotlight is the recognition card in the dashboard's People section; publishing replaces the current one (only one is active at a time), and its congratulations thread notifies the person recognized.\n- **Delete** — tap twice to confirm.\n\nThere's no approve/decline queue — nothing posts publicly unless you make it the Spotlight.\n" },
  { file: "admin/quick-links.md", raw: "---\ntitle: Managing quick links\naudience: admin\nroute: /admin/quick-links\n---\n\n[Manage Quick Links](/admin/quick-links) owns the org-wide link catalog that feeds the phone Quick Links dock, the desktop Systems menu, the utility-bar system links, the dashboard featured-tiles picker, and global search.\n\n**Add link:** Label, Subtitle, URL, Category (free text with suggestions), Icon (a Lucide icon name — falls back to a generic link icon), **Sort order** (lower = first within its category), **Visible to** (crew/supervisor/admin — all unchecked means everyone), and **Active**.\n\nRows are grouped by category with Deactivate, Edit, and Delete. Reordering is by the sort-order number — there's no drag-and-drop. Changes reach everyone's dashboard in real time.\n\nNotes: crew pin their personal favorites in the dock themselves, and pick their own featured tiles — you manage the catalog, not their choices. Some tiles are matched by exact label (the role-default featured tiles, the \"Patient Referral Form\" used by the MIH page, \"Employee Shoutout\") — renaming those labels breaks the match, so keep names stable.\n" },
  { file: "admin/usage.md", raw: "---\ntitle: Usage dashboard\naudience: admin\nroute: /admin/usage\n---\n\n[Usage](/admin/usage) shows how the agency actually uses the portal, from page views logged on every route change (times in Central).\n\nPanels: roster size and \"ever signed in\" reach; active users over 30 days / 7 days / 24 hours; views this week vs last; people-per-day and page-views-per-day charts (30 days); time-of-day pattern with the peak hour; engagement depth (power users with 15+ active days, regulars, occasional, dormant — with names — and never signed in); \"where the time goes\" by section; top pages; most engaged people; and a per-person drill-down of pages used and daily activity.\n\nUse it to spot who never adopted the portal (the dormant and never-signed-in lists) and which features carry the traffic. Tracking is route-level only — it doesn't record individual clicks or form activity.\n" },
  { file: "admin/badge-maker.md", raw: "---\ntitle: Badge maker\naudience: admin\nroute: /admin/badge-maker\n---\n\n[Badge Maker](/admin/badge-maker) designs and prints CR80 employee ID cards (2.125 × 3.370 in) sized for direct printing on the Badgy card printer. It's a full-screen tool with its own roster, saved automatically so any admin can reprint from any machine.\n\nPer card: name, title, badge number, expiration and issue dates, provider level with its accent/band color, a photo with zoom and position controls, and back-of-card certification numbers (Texas DSHS, RN/BON, NREMT) plus agency settings (medical director, return address).\n\nRoster controls: Add person, Duplicate, Delete, and Save/Load roster file for JSON backups. Printing: **Print front**, **Print back**, or **Print both**, with a \"Slot-punched cards\" toggle that keeps the punch area clear.\n\nNote its roster is its own list — it doesn't read from Manage Employees, so new hires are added here manually when their badge is made.\n" },
  { file: "admin/exams.md", raw: "---\ntitle: Running protocol exams (editors)\naudience: admin\nroute: /clinical/exams\n---\n\n[Exams](/clinical/exams) (clinical editors) manages proctored protocol examinations: \"Assign → release when the candidate is seated → auto-graded on submit.\"\n\n1. Pick the exam, choose the candidate in **Assign to…**, and **Assign**. The candidate sees it on their My Progress page, locked.\n2. When they're seated, hit **Release** under Open assignments — their page unlocks live and the clock starts when they begin.\n3. Grading is automatic and server-side (answer keys never reach the browser). Results show score, pass/fail, any critical items missed (informational — they don't block a pass), and a **Completed exam** PDF with the candidate's answers (wrong ones marked, no answer key).\n\nA pass auto-checks the candidate's protocol gate and files a completion certificate to their documents. The credentialing checklist surfaces alongside each assignment, and **Run a megacode** opens the digital megacode evaluation sheet (examiner script, scoring sections, dual signatures — a pass checks the megacode gate and files the signed PDF).\n\nExam content itself isn't edited in the UI — question sets are loaded through the controlled import, so changes go through the CDO.\n" },
  { file: "admin/protocols-manage.md", raw: "---\ntitle: Managing protocol content\naudience: admin\nroute: /admin/protocols\n---\n\n[Manage Protocols](/admin/protocols) edits the live protocol content. Reach it from the Protocols app → **More** tab → **Admin** (it's not in the Admin menu).\n\nPick a protocol from the dropdown, then edit its criteria (Adult / Pediatric / general notes) and the step lists per level — add steps, warnings, branching conditions, and medical-control items — then **Save Protocol**.\n\nImportant characteristics:\n\n- **Changes go live immediately** — there's no draft or approval step. Online users see the new text on their next load; devices using Download-for-Offline keep their cached copy until they reconnect or re-download.\n- Only protocol *content* is editable here: names/numbers/categories, procedure body text, the medication reference, the formulary, the equipment list, and the tools have no in-app editor — those changes go through the protocol book process with the CDO.\n\nGiven protocol text is medical direction, treat this page with the same care as the printed book: coordinate edits with the Medical Director and announce meaningful changes (Required Training video + skills verification was the 2026 pattern).\n" },
  { file: "admin/scheduling-admin.md", raw: "---\ntitle: Scheduling administration\naudience: admin\nroute: /schedule\n---\n\nScheduling admin lives inside [Schedule](/schedule) under the **Manage** menu. Editing power belongs to the **Global admin** and **Scheduler** access levels — a portal admin defaults to only Supervisor-level schedule access until granted more.\n\n- **Access grants:** Members → open a person → the **Access** dropdown (Global admins only): Scheduler, Supervisor (can send page-outs), HR (payroll only), View only, No access. The same panel sets credential overrides, position qualifications, unit exclusions, and \"Hide from scheduling\".\n- **Units & seats:** Setup → \"Units & display order\" — add units (code, label, station, seat preset), set each unit's rotation (agency default 48/96 B-B-C-C-A-A or a custom pattern) and daily shift hours, reorder, deactivate.\n- **Rotation template:** Setup → \"Rotation template — who holds each seat, per shift\". Click a cell, type a name, set the **Effective** date (clashes offer Swap / Move only). This table is also what drives everyone's profile shift/station and the GAL office field — change seats here, never on profiles.\n- **Approvals:** the Requests tab is the work queue — time off, pickups, extra hours, trades, and time discrepancies, with Approve / Deny / Edit times.\n- **Events:** click a day → \"Add a special event\" (name, window, Paramedic/Attendant seat counts, location, double-time toggle). Event rosters can drive event-tied required training.\n- **Page-outs:** compose push/email/text blasts, optionally attaching open shifts, to a filtered roster.\n- **Payroll:** Time Reports → Verify punches, Hours, Paycom export, Sign-offs, Balances; Setup → \"Paycom earning codes\" (Global admin/HR) maps categories to codes.\n- Day tools: \"+ Add to this day\" (events, notes, students, extra seats, record time off / extra hours) and the person editor (change times, mark off, move, replace).\n" },
  { file: "admin/pipeline.md", raw: "---\ntitle: Clinical pipeline — advancing people (editors)\naudience: admin\nroute: /clinical\n---\n\nCredentialing is run from the [Clinical Development console](/clinical) by **clinical editors** — a separate grant list from portal admin (managed via the Editors panel on the legacy board). The phase ladder: NEOP Academy → Field Training Rotation (FTR) → P1 Attendant → P2 In-Charge, plus the opt-in P3 FTO ride-up track and an AEMT upgrade track.\n\nDay to day: **Today** is the work queue (field-training queue, expiring/expired credentials, classes to schedule, Action Center), **Board** is the all-member compliance grid with CSV export, and **People** opens each employee file (licensure, cards, gates, field training, exams, megacodes, documents, messages).\n\n**Advancing someone:** on the trainee's card, **\"Advance to <next phase>\"** opens the Phase Advancement Record — verify the four certifications, document a waiver if the phase is under its day minimum, set the next phase's start date and FTO, capture the **employee's signature**, and **Sign as CDO & advance**. The record PDF files to their documents automatically, and an FTO change triggers the trainee's FTO evaluation. On the employee file, Actions also offers program-track enrollment, **Promote — clear <phase>**, full record editing, and clinical-tracking exclusion.\n\nThe **accelerated P2 pathway** (10-day standard vs the traditional 36) is a checkbox in Edit full record; the card then shows \"P1 → P2 · accelerated\".\n\nAdvancement ripples outward automatically: the scheduler's credential derivation follows the phase immediately, and the person's GAL job title updates on the next daily sync.\n" },
  { file: "admin/assistant-admin.md", raw: "---\ntitle: Ask WCEMS assistant — admin view\naudience: admin\nroute: /admin/assistant\n---\n\n[Assistant](/admin/assistant) is the visibility page for this assistant. Two tabs:\n\n- **Questions** — month-to-date question count and estimated API spend, plus the recent exchange log: who asked what, when, the answer (expandable), and per-exchange token counts and cost. Every answered question is logged automatically.\n- **Requests** — the feature-request inbox. When the assistant can't answer something, the asker can send it to the dev team (there's also a quiet \"Suggest a feature\" link in the panel); each request lands here with the verbatim question and any note. Triage with **Kind** (feature / docs gap / bug / other), **Status** (new / planned / done / declined), and an internal admin note — new ones are badged.\n\nOperating notes: users are limited to 40 questions a day. Answers come from a curated knowledge base about the intranet **plus live lookups** — schedule and who's on duty, leave balances, pending requests, outstanding training/policies, directory, hospitals, classes, announcements, equipment status, and verbatim protocol/medication text from the protocol book. Every lookup runs under the asker's own permissions, so the assistant can never show someone more than the app itself would, and it structurally cannot return door codes. It quotes protocols verbatim but never gives medical advice, and it declines HR topics by design. The knowledge base ships with the app — updating it is a developer task (see docs/assistant.md in the repo).\n" },
]
